1
00:00:03,052 --> 00:00:05,259
Every evening, the Sun goes down,

2
00:00:05,309 --> 00:00:06,422
and it gets dark.

3
00:00:06,472 --> 00:00:08,405
Every morning, it comes back.

4
00:00:08,455 --> 00:00:10,234
Where does it go at night?

5
00:00:11,079 --> 00:00:12,185
Mila has an idea:

6
00:00:12,235 --> 00:00:14,549
the Sun switches off, like a lamp!

7
00:00:15,372 --> 00:00:18,255
Curio takes a look: in the middle of the night,

8
00:00:18,305 --> 00:00:20,815
the Sun is still shining, just as bright.

9
00:00:20,865 --> 00:00:22,188
It never switches off.

10
00:00:22,238 --> 00:00:22,425
So?

11
00:00:23,212 --> 00:00:24,726
Discovery mission!

12
00:00:28,214 --> 00:00:29,594
From here, it's clear:

13
00:00:29,644 --> 00:00:32,973
the Sun always lights up only one half of the Earth.

14
00:00:33,023 --> 00:00:34,972
The other half is in the dark.

15
00:00:35,750 --> 00:00:37,468
And the Earth spins on itself,

16
00:00:37,518 --> 00:00:39,236
like a very slow spinning top.

17
00:00:39,286 --> 00:00:42,291
One full turn takes a whole day: twenty-four hours.

18
00:00:43,795 --> 00:00:46,343
Look at this little dot: it's your home.

19
00:00:46,393 --> 00:00:49,136
When it turns toward the Sun, it's morning.

20
00:00:49,186 --> 00:00:50,111
Then afternoon.

21
00:00:50,161 --> 00:00:52,124
Then it moves to the dark side…

22
00:00:52,174 --> 00:00:53,148
and it's night.

23
00:00:53,932 --> 00:00:55,532
The Sun doesn't really rise:

24
00:00:55,582 --> 00:00:57,534
we are the ones turning toward it.

25
00:00:57,584 --> 00:00:59,1000
But it comes back every morning, promise.

26
00:01:00,808 --> 00:01:03,218
That's why there is day, then night.

27
00:01:04,849 --> 00:01:06,500
The Earth spins on itself:

28
00:01:06,550 --> 00:01:09,365
when your side faces the Sun, it's daytime.

29
00:01:10,199 --> 00:01:12,262
With an adult: in the dark,

30
00:01:12,312 --> 00:01:14,845
a lamp and an orange on a pencil.

31
00:01:14,895 --> 00:01:17,741
Stick on a dot, turn the orange: day…

32
00:01:17,791 --> 00:01:18,211
night…

33
00:01:18,261 --> 00:01:18,574
day!

34
00:01:19,361 --> 00:01:21,311
And how does a rainbow form?

35
00:01:21,361 --> 00:01:22,789
The answer tomorrow.
